  "notes": "USAGE:\nMost commonly encountered in news and weather reports about pollen season ({花粉|かふん}{飛散|ひさん}). Also used for debris from explosions, accidents, or construction. Used as a suru-verb ({飛散|ひさん}する).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {花粉|かふん}{飛散|ひさん} (pollen dispersal)\n- {飛散|ひさん}{防止|ぼうし} (prevention of scattering)\n- {飛散|ひさん}{量|りょう} (amount of dispersal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {散乱|さんらん}: scattering, being strewn about — for objects on the ground rather than in the air\n- {拡散|かくさん}: diffusion, spreading — broader dispersal over a wider area",
